; 10 - Byte order mark   ; ERROR: an invisible BOM stands before this line
; Some editors (e.g. Notepad in older Windows versions) start a UTF-8 file
; with a byte order mark (BOM). VS Code hides it - the status bar says
; "UTF-8 with BOM". qaflisp reads it as part of line 1 and reports
; "Illegal mnemonic"; if line 1 were "ORG $20", the ORG would be lost.
;
; Try it:
;   - Click "UTF-8 with BOM" in the status bar, "Save with Encoding",
;     "UTF-8": the error in line 1 disappears (or use the quick fix).
;     git checkout restores the example.

            ORG     $20             ; OK
Start       LDA     #1              ; OK
            STA     $FB             ; OK
            BRA     Start           ; OK
            END
